@startuml
title Terraform v2 - separate ownership cleanup (OC-19)
autonumber
actor "Authorized operator / independent test supervisor" as Caller
control ResourceCleanupService as Cleanup
control EnvironmentOperationManager as Operations
database "Instance / Attempt / State metadata" as Records
boundary TerraformExecutor as Terraform
boundary "AWS / Kubernetes read verification" as Provider
Caller -> Cleanup: Cleanup(confirmed user set OR explicit authorized run IDs)
Cleanup -> Operations: Admit Environment owner/fence; prior process stopped
Cleanup -> Records: Load module/state/ownership/consumer/dependency evidence
Records --> Cleanup: pinned resources + classification
Cleanup -> Cleanup: Reject foreign/platform/external-consumer; run mode also rejects preexisting/updated
loop Reverse dependency, consumers first
  Cleanup -> Terraform: DESTROY with original module/target and state lock
  Terraform --> Cleanup: result + durable terminal state
  Cleanup -> Provider: Confirm physical IDs/tags absent
  Provider --> Cleanup: absence / remaining IDs / verification error
  Cleanup -> Records: Persist per-resource cleanup proof / remaining IDs
end
alt all authorized resources verified absent
  Cleanup -> Records: SUCCEEDED; retain state tombstones/audit
else resources remaining or unknown
  Cleanup -> Records: FAILED / INTERRUPTED; preserve handles and remaining IDs
end
Cleanup -> Operations: Release only when old subprocess stopped; otherwise hold
Cleanup --> Caller: verified completion / incomplete cleanup
note over Caller, Cleanup
Browser/runner failure does not terminate independent supervisor.
No namespace/account wildcard deletion; cleanup is not data rollback.
end note
@enduml
